Provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unlike this repository's Python, Go and Node.js bindings -- which adapt SAP's
own Apache-2.0 licensed clients -- **no upstream code was adapted here.**

RSAP, the abandoned predecessor, cannot be adapted: its DESCRIPTION declares
`License: GPL-3`, its README refers instead to the LGPL by way of a COPYING
file that does not exist in the repository, and `src/RSAP.c` -- the file one
would most want to learn from -- carries only "Copyright (c) 2012 - and onwards
Piers Harding. All rights reserved." with no grant at all.

The two predecessors for Ruby and R carry no permissive licence grant:

  * piersharding/ruby-sapnwrfc has no LICENSE file and no `license` field in
    its gemspec. Its README says only "Released under Ruby's License", by an
    undated reference.
  * piersharding/RSAP declares `License: GPL-3` in DESCRIPTION, while its C
    source carries "All rights reserved" and no grant at all.

Neither was read while implementing this package, and no code from either appears
in it. The API is designed for modern Ruby rather than reproducing theirs.

The RFC protocol itself is implemented in Rust in `erpl-proto`, whose
specification is derived solely from this project's own packet captures of
SAP's `libsapnwrfc` -- never by reading another implementation's source. Other
implementations are used only as running black boxes, to compare behaviour
against; `examples/run_both.sh` is that technique mechanised.

